WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.218
Hi! We see rectangles and squares every day: doors, windows, books and tiles. Today let's look closely at their properties and use them to solve problems.

2
00:00:13.368 --> 00:00:20.010
A rectangle has 4 sides, and all 4 angles are right angles, which means 90 degrees.

3
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:26.466
Opposite sides are equal in length: the top and bottom are the same, and so are the two sides.

4
00:00:26.616 --> 00:00:32.418
Opposite sides are parallel, like railway tracks that never meet.

5
00:00:32.568 --> 00:00:40.650
A square is a special rectangle: it also has 4 right angles and parallel opposite sides, and all 4 sides are equal.

6
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:54.858
To draw one on grid paper, follow the grid lines and count the squares, and the corners will be right angles. For example, a rectangle 5 squares by 3 squares, or a square with sides of 4 squares.

7
00:00:55.008 --> 00:00:57.858
ABCD is a rectangle.

8
00:00:58.008 --> 00:01:04.530
A line is drawn from B to point E on AD. Angle ABE is 35 degrees.

9
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:11.106
What is angle EBC? Angle B of the rectangle is a right angle, 90 degrees.

10
00:01:11.256 --> 00:01:18.138
So angle EBC is 90 minus 35, which is 55 degrees.

11
00:01:18.288 --> 00:01:23.538
Watch out! A shape with 4 equal sides is not always a square!

12
00:01:23.688 --> 00:01:31.938
If you push a square over, the sides stay the same length, but the angles are no longer right angles, so it isn't a square any more.

13
00:01:32.088 --> 00:01:37.506
A square needs 4 equal sides and 4 right angles.

14
00:01:37.656 --> 00:01:48.834
Your turn! A square has a perimeter of 24 cm. How long is each side? Pause and think.

15
00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:57.594
A square's 4 sides are equal, so 24 divided by 4 is 6 cm. Did you get it right?

16
00:01:57.744 --> 00:02:11.370
Another one! A line splits a corner of a rectangle into two parts. One part is 28 degrees. What is the other part? Pause and think.

17
00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:21.114
A rectangle's corner is 90 degrees. 90 minus 28 is 62 degrees. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:21.264 --> 00:02:32.682
Last one! In rectangle PQRS, PQ is 9 cm. How long is SR? Pause and think.

19
00:02:32.832 --> 00:02:41.466
SR is opposite PQ, and opposite sides are equal, so it's also 9 cm. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:41.616 --> 00:02:55.554
Remember: a rectangle has 4 right angles, and its opposite sides are equal and parallel. A square also has 4 equal sides. To find an unknown angle, use the fact that a right angle is 90 degrees.

21
00:02:55.704 --> 00:03:00.162
Look for rectangles and squares at home!

